<title>USA: SoundScan releases 1996 music industry figures.</title>
<headline>SoundScan releases 1996 music industry figures.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>SoundScan, the entertainment industry's data information system which tracks point-of-purchase sales of recorded music product, Monday announced its 1996 year-end sales research data as follows:</p>
<p>			1996 TOP-TEN SELLING ALBUMS</p>
<p>				    (Year-To-Date)</p>
<p>1.  Alanis Morissette / Jagged Little Pill	   7.4 Million</p>
<p>2.  Celine Dion / Falling Into You		     6.1 Million</p>
<p>3.  Fugees / Score					   4.5 Million</p>
<p>4.  No Doubt / Tragic Kingdom			    4.4 Million</p>
<p>5.  Mariah Carey / Daydream				3.1 Million</p>
<p>6.  2 Pac / All Eyez On Me				 3.0 Million</p>
<p>7.  Metallica / Load					 3.0 Million</p>
<p>8.  Toni Braxton / Secrets				 2.9 Million</p>
<p>9.  Shania Twain / Woman In Me			   2.8 Million</p>
<p>10. Oasis / What's The Story Morning Glory	   2.6 Million</p>
<p>		  1996 YEAR-TO-DATE RECORD COMPANY MARKET SHARE</p>
<p>				  (1/1/96 - 12/29/96)</p>
<p>Total Albums		 Current Albums	     Singles</p>
<p>(Catalog &amp;</p>
<p>Current Titles)</p>
<p>WEA     21.1		 WEA    20.9		  WEA    19.7</p>
<p>BMG     10.7		 BMG    12.5		  BMG    27.8</p>
<p>UNI     10.6		 UNI    11.4		  UNI     9.3</p>
<p>PGD     13.1		 PGD    11.4		  PGD    15.4</p>
<p>EMD	8.7		 EMD     8.2		  EMD     4.2</p>
<p>SONY    14.7		 SONY   15.3		  SONY   12.4</p>
<p>OTHERS  21.2		 OTHERS 20.3		  OTHERS 11.2</p>
<p>				   TOTAL ALBUM SALES</p>
<p>		    (Includes Catalog And Current Titles)</p>
<p>				   1996		  1995</p>
<p>Albums		     616.6 Million     616.3 Million</p>
<p>CDs			  448.4 Million     409.5 Million</p>
<p>Cassettes		  166.7 Million     205.8 Million</p>
<p>Other			  1.5 Million	 1.0 Million</p>
